malized pairings","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:51b287e91dfe4a6e90a8facfcd90b07d47d4b9beab1260ae70316f43bad63046","file":"preprints/Riesz-transforms-and-uniform-rectifiability-in-higher-codimension-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":61,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1269085c430642d1e695650f6c5b696d03c395d8838d18935ad68c55e617fc4a","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Riesz-transforms-and-uniform-rectifiability-in-higher-codimension-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:51b287e91dfe4a6e90a8facfcd90b07d47d4b9beab1260ae70316f43bad63046","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Riesz-transforms-and-uniform-rectifiability-in-higher-codimension-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L61"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $d\\ge4$ and $2\\le n\\le d-2$ be integers. Let $\\mu$ be an\n$n$-Ahlfors--David regular Radon measure on $\\R^d$ satisfying\n\\eqref{eq:riesz-bound}. Then $\\mu$ is uniformly $n$-rectifiable in the\nsense of Definition~\\ref{def:ur}. Its constants $\\theta$ and $M$ can\nbe chosen in terms of $d,n,C_{\\rm AD}$ and $C_{\\rm R}$ alone."}
